# Lesson 2, from the point-count exercise hand 3 (a diamond added: the PDF hand has 12 cards).
title: Open 1NT, partner bids game
id: L02-03
type: exercise
lesson: 2
concepts: 2.2, 2.4
student: S
board: 3
dealer: S
vulnerable: EW

deal:            # spades  hearts  diamonds  clubs
  N  Q85    A93    K763   Q83
  E  A962   Q7     T95    A942
  S  KJ7    KT82   AQ42   K6
  W  T43    J654   J8     JT75

auction:
  S 1NT*   = 15-17 points, balanced
     key: 16 HCP and balanced: open 1NT.
     not 1D: Did you count 16? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT, not one of a suit.
     not 1H: Did you count 16? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT, not one of a suit.
     not 1C: Did you count 16? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT, not one of a suit.
     not Pass: Did you count your points? 16 is plenty to open.
     not *: Did you count 16? A balanced 15-17 opens 1NT.
  W Pass
  N 3NT    = 10+ points, balanced: game
  E Pass
  S Pass*  = Partner has chosen the game
     key: Partner knows your range and has picked the contract. Pass.
     not *: Partner knew you have 15-17 and chose game. Is there anything left to tell her?
  W Pass

auction recap:
  Your 1NT told partner almost everything: 15-17 points and a balanced
  hand. With 10 or more points, she knew your side had at least 25, so she
  bid game. You are declarer, because you bid no-trump first, and so West
  will lead to the first trick.

planning:
  remind: What is the contract? How many tricks do you need?

play:
  1   W CJ  N C3  E C2  S CK
  2   S SK  W S3  N S5  E SA
      note: The plan: take four diamonds, two spades and two hearts to go with your club trick. First drive out the ♠A.
  3   E D5  S DQ  W D8  N D3
  4   S D2  W DJ  N DK  E D9
      note: Now the diamonds: over to dummy's ♦K.
  5   N D6  E DT  S DA  W S4
      note: Back to your ♦A.
  6   S H2  W H4  N H9  E HQ
      note: Lead a heart to set up a second heart trick.
  7   E S2  S S7  W ST  N SQ
  8   N S8  E S9  S SJ  W C5
      note: A spade back to your ♠J.
  9   S D4  W C7  N D7  E C4
      note: Dummy's last diamond is a winner.
  10  N HA  E H7  S H8  W H5
      note: The ♥A.
  11  N H3  E S6  S HK  W H6
      note: A heart to your ♥K.
  12  S C6  W CT  N CQ  E CA
      note: A club to dummy's ♣Q. East's ace takes it.
  13  E C9  S HT  W HJ  N C8
      note: 9 tricks: 3NT made.

play recap:
  The plan: drive out the ♠A, then take four diamonds, two spades and two
  hearts to go with your club trick.

  3NT made. Your side had 27 points and balanced hands, just what no-trump
  games are made of.
